ugh to feed his three monkeys for a week.\nOne monkey eats 10 bananas each day.\nSo the first monkey eats 10 bananas each day.\nThe second monkey eats 4 more bananas than the first monkey.\nSo the second monkey eats 10 + 4 = 14 bananas each day.\nThe third monkey eats the rest of the bananas for the day.\nSo the third monkey eats 315 - 10 - 14 = 291 bananas each day.\nThe answer is 291.\n\nAnswer_33:\nAnswer_33:\nTeddy finished half of a 500 piece puzzle.\nSo he finished 500 / 2 = 250 pieces.\nHe then started and finished another 500 piece puzzle.\nSo he finished 500 more pieces.\nIn total, he finished 250 + 500 = 750 pieces.\nThe answer is 750.\n\nAnswer_34:\nAnswer_34:\nJenny bought 15 roses.\nRoses cost $2 each.\nSo she paid 15 * $2 = $30 for the roses.\nShe paid with 5 $5 bills.\nSo she paid with $25.\nShe got $5 in change.\nSo she left with $5.\nThe answer is 5.\n\nAnswer_35:\nAnswer_35:\nTerry sells 6 milkshakes for $5.50 each.\nSo he makes 6 * $5.50 = $33 from milkshakes.\nHe sells 9 burger platters for $11 each.\nSo he makes 9 * $11 = $99 from burger platters.\nHe sells 20 sodas for $1.50 each.\nSo he makes 20 * $1.50 = $30 from sodas.\nIn total, he makes $33 + $99 + $30 = $162.\nThe answer is 162.\n\nAnswer_36:\nAnswer_36:\nPaul is waiting for his train at the station.\nThe fourth train scheduled to arrive at the station is the one he needs to get on.\nThe first train is scheduled to arrive in 10 minutes.\nThe second train is scheduled to arrive 20 minutes after the first train.\nSo the second train is scheduled to arrive in 10 + 20 = 30 minutes.\nThe third train is scheduled to arrive 20 minutes after the second train.\nSo the third train is scheduled to arrive in 30 + 20 = 50 minutes.\nThe fourth train is scheduled to arrive 20 minutes after the third train.\nSo the fourth train is scheduled to arrive in 50 + 20 = 70 minutes.\nIn total, Paul will wait 70 minutes.\nThe answer is 70.\n\nAnswer_37:\nAnswer_37:\nMelanie has 10 toothpicks each week.\nShe has 1